<title>UK: BASKETBALL-EUROLEAGUE STANDINGS. [CORRECTED 23:04 GMT]</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-EUROLEAGUE STANDINGS. [CORRECTED 23:04 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standings after Thursday's games</p>
<p>in men's EuroLeague basketball (tabulate under played, won,</p>
<p>lost, points)</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p> Stefanel Milan (Italy)	5  4  1  9</p>
<p> Maccabi Tel Aviv (Israel)   5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Ulker Spor (Turkey)	   5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Panionios (Greece)	    5  2  3  7</p>
<p> CSKA Moscow (Russia)	  5  2  3  7</p>
<p> Limoges (France)		5  1  4  6</p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p> Olympiakos (Greece)	   5  4  1  9</p>
<p> Teamsystem Bologna (Italy)  5  4  1  9</p>
<p> Cibona Zagreb (Croatia)     5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Estudiantes Madrid (Spain)  5  2  3  7</p>
<p> Alba Berlin (Germany)	 5  2  3  7</p>
<p> Charleroi (Belgium)	   5  0  5  5</p>
<p>Group C</p>
<p> Villeurbanne (France)	 5  4  1  9</p>
<p> Barcelona (Spain)	     5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Panathinaikos (Greece)	5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Ljubljana (Slovenia)	  5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Split (Croatia)		 5  2  3  7</p>
<p> Bayer Leverkusen (Germany)  5  0  5  5</p>
<p>(Correction switches Ljubljana and Split records, which were transposed).</p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p> Virtus Bologna (Italy)	   5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Efes Pilsen (Turkey)	     5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Pau-Orthez (France)		5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Partizan Belgrade (Yugoslavia) 5  3  2  8</p>
<p> Sevilla (Spain)		    5  2  3  7</p>
<p> Dynamo Moscow (Russia)	   5  1  4  6</p>
</text>
